<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theobald I of Blois</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 975</span> · Also known as Theobald the Trickster</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theobald I of Blois (died 975), known as the Trickster, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-the-great">Hugh the Great</a> who by about 940 held the counties of Blois, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Chartres</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>. He married Luitgard, daughter of Herbert II of Vermandois, and founded the house of Blois, whose counts rivalled the early Capetians. His grandson Odo II added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troyes">Troyes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meaux">Meaux</a>.</p></div>
